  "question": {
    "text": "Given below are two statements:</p><p>Statement (I) : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SiO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>GeO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> are acidic while <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>SnO</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>PbO</mi></math> are amphoteric in nature.<br/>Statement (II) : Allotropic forms of carbon are due to property of catenation and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pπ</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>dπ</mi></math> bond formation.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "dZZ5v",
      "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are false",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "VzzBD",
      "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are true",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "16LK8",
      "text": "Statement I is true but Statement II is false",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "841tB",
      "text": "Statement I is true but Statement II is true",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Statement I,</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>SnO</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>PbO</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><msub><mi>SnO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><msub><mi>PbO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo> </mo><mo>:</mo><mo> </mo><mtext>Amphoteric</mtext><mo> </mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><msub><mi>SiO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><msub><mi>GeO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>GeO</mi><mo> </mo><mo>:</mo><mo> </mo><mtext>Acidic</mtext><mo> </mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mi>CO</mi><mo> </mo><mo>:</mo><mtext> Neutral</mtext></math></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">According to Statement II,<br/>Carbon does not have d-orbitals so can not form <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pπ</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>dπ</mi></math> Bond with itself. Due to properties of catenation and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pπ</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>pπ</mi></math> bond formation, carbon is able to show allotropic forms. Allotropic forms of carbon can be crystalline and amorphous.<br/>Diamond and graphite are two well-known crystalline forms of carbon. </p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Hence option C is the answer.</p>",
